						<td width="100%" class="body" valign="top">
														Death of a Guild Member<br />
 <br />
<br />
On 10-21-01, the day of our get together in West Free, I noticed that everyone was dueling each other at the end of the gathering. I was asked to dual with Shim, (she was green to me). I accepted the dual, knowing I could probably kill her with one to three kicks. I had no intention of actually fighting Shim. I thought that maybe she needed to practice with her 1hb with her whip. I never engaged my attack mode or clicked my kick hot button at all, at any time, whatsoever. So as the honorable monk that I am, I continued to do nothing, and just stood there. All I saw on the text screen was Shim tries to slash Maktar, but misses, over &amp; over again. I had a smirky smile on my face, remembering the pain of the &quot;training lvl's&quot;, ...... and I just stood there. I received /tells from others wanting to know if I was o.k., and what's going on, as most know, I really enjoy a fight. I told them what was going on........ and just stood there. After ten to fifteen minutes, I'm still &quot;just standing there&quot;.<br />
At lvl 35, monks get a skill called &quot;Riposote&quot;. Riposote can be defined as: Automatically blocking a hit and counter attacking with his/her own hit, (in battle, it's an &quot;extra&quot; attack :-). Again, this is done automatically. I chatted some more, got up and grabbed a drink. When i returned, to my surprise, Shim lost a lot of hp's. I scrolled up and saw my Riposote kicked in a couple of times. I was thinking, ~~~man, I hope she zones or stops attacking~~~. I grabbed my mouse and backed up, but I was too late, I heard the god awful sound. The sound of Shim dying at my feet. My heart sank to about my ankles.<br />
The moral of the story is:<br />
#1. If you ever dual, make sure they are blue in color, there is a healer near, you are super buffed, or you are by a zone. <br />
#2. Know when to zone and when to stop when dueling friends.<br />
#3. Never grab a Pepsi when dueling.<br />
<br />
Some guild members know me and know that I will always be the first to &quot;take a death&quot; in  battle. As a monk, I have Fein Death. I have waited for the very last minute to engage FD when in a groups, and at times, &quot;peel and die&quot; so other can run to safety. I will never intentionally be the cause of the sight of a guild members corps laying in front of my feet. But I will die for a guild member, just give me a /tell, and I'm there with ya.<br />
~sorry you died Shim~<br />
<br />
-----Maktar (Noble Alliance)						</td>
